# ── Media uploads (server fallback) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional. When a user does NOT configure their own Cloudinary or S3 account in
# Settings → Media & uploads, BNOS can upload media through this server and
# forward it to Cloudinary (signing server-side so the secret never reaches the
# browser). Leave blank to keep BNOS fully local-first with no server uploads.
#
# You need BNOS_CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME plus either:
#   • BNOS_CLOUDINARY_UPLOAD_PRESET for unsigned uploads, or
#   • BNOS_CLOUDINARY_API_KEY + BNOS_CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET for signed uploads
#
# Uploads are organized into folders like:
#   <BNOS_CLOUDINARY_FOLDER>/bnos/<orgId|anonymous>/<purpose>
BNOS_CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME=
BNOS_CLOUDINARY_API_KEY=
BNOS_CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET=
BNOS_CLOUDINARY_UPLOAD_PRESET=
BNOS_CLOUDINARY_FOLDER=bnos
